00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.982
- One of the things you
would want to be sure to do

00:00:30.982 --> 00:00:35.478
is, whether you like it or
not, get very comfortable,

00:00:35.478 --> 00:00:38.074
it make take awhile, with
public speaking, for example.

00:00:38.074 --> 00:00:42.241
I mean, that's a asset that
will last you 50 or 60 years,

00:00:43.563 --> 00:00:46.125
and it's a liability if
you don't like doing it,

00:00:46.125 --> 00:00:47.065
or are uncomfortable doing it.

00:00:47.065 --> 00:00:49.079
That also will last you 50 or 60 years,

00:00:49.079 --> 00:00:50.544
and it's a necessary skill.

00:00:50.544 --> 00:00:52.442
- So I'm a big fan of public speaking.

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:55.476
I think if you can learn how to speak,

00:00:55.476 --> 00:00:58.995
it can dramatically improve the abilities

00:00:58.995 --> 00:01:01.588
to communicate your ideas,
to get your message across,

00:01:01.588 --> 00:01:03.873
to grow your business, to build a team.

00:01:03.873 --> 00:01:07.271
But I don't know that I would
call it a necessary skill.

00:01:07.271 --> 00:01:10.756
I think whatever it is
that you want to do,

00:01:10.756 --> 00:01:13.234
you need to be able to bring
people on board to your idea.

00:01:13.234 --> 00:01:15.155
Right, as an entrepreneur
it's really really hard

00:01:15.155 --> 00:01:17.592
to have success just being a solo person.

00:01:17.592 --> 00:01:19.702
So you need to be able
to communicate your idea

00:01:19.702 --> 00:01:23.274
to one on one people, to group settings,

00:01:23.274 --> 00:01:25.257
and then to large group settings,

00:01:25.257 --> 00:01:28.037
and your ability to be
able to do that well

00:01:28.037 --> 00:01:30.823
will help you grow a lot faster.

00:01:30.823 --> 00:01:33.955
If you can't communicate your
ideas very well to people,

00:01:33.955 --> 00:01:36.251
it's going to be a lot
harder to get your project

00:01:36.251 --> 00:01:37.840
off the ground.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.461
That being said, and again
this is something that I do

00:01:40.461 --> 00:01:43.893
for a living, right, I
massively appreciate the value

00:01:43.893 --> 00:01:46.418
of being able to communicate
ideas and be a public speaker.

00:01:46.418 --> 00:01:50.210
But that being said, it's
not the only way to win.

00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:52.074
I wouldn't call it a necessary skill,

00:01:52.074 --> 00:01:53.887
because there's a lot of
other ways that you can stand,

00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:55.092
there's a lot of other ways to win.

00:01:55.092 --> 00:01:56.864
There's tons of people
who you've never heard of

00:01:56.864 --> 00:02:00.692
who are billionaires who
suck at public speaking.

00:02:00.692 --> 00:02:03.067
The thing is though, if
that's going to be something

00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:06.178
that you ignore, then you
have to really really really

00:02:06.178 --> 00:02:07.455
be great at something else.

00:02:07.455 --> 00:02:10.481
You have to be off the charts
amazing at something else.

00:02:10.481 --> 00:02:13.135
If you are a really poor
public communicator,

00:02:13.135 --> 00:02:17.807
then you better be insanely
good at something else.

00:02:17.807 --> 00:02:20.509
And so it brings me back
to that teaching a rabbit

00:02:20.509 --> 00:02:23.041
how to swim versus how
to hop, you know rabbits

00:02:23.041 --> 00:02:25.414
are great at hopping and suck at swimming

00:02:25.414 --> 00:02:27.243
and if you try to teach
a rabbit how to swim,

00:02:27.243 --> 00:02:29.149
they're going to be average at best.

00:02:29.149 --> 00:02:30.820
If you just say, forget about swimming,

00:02:30.820 --> 00:02:33.764
focus on hopping, you could
be really really really great.

00:02:33.764 --> 00:02:36.847
And so is that equivalent in
your life and your business

00:02:36.847 --> 00:02:39.235
for you, your talents, your skillsets.

00:02:39.235 --> 00:02:43.162
What's the hopping for you,
and ignoring the swimming part.

00:02:43.162 --> 00:02:46.057
I think it's a skill that
everybody should at least try,

00:02:46.057 --> 00:02:49.098
you shouldn't just write it
off and say this isn't for me,

00:02:49.098 --> 00:02:51.259
this sucks, I'm never going
to be a great speaker.

00:02:51.259 --> 00:02:53.911
I think it's a good skillset
if you can develop it

00:02:53.911 --> 00:02:55.706
and so it's worth giving a shot.

00:02:55.706 --> 00:02:57.716
Just like entrepreneurship,
I think everybody

00:02:57.716 --> 00:03:00.553
should at least try to get that idea

00:03:00.553 --> 00:03:02.559
that they have in their head out there.

00:03:02.559 --> 00:03:05.158
At least try to be an entrepreneur
before writing it off.

00:03:05.158 --> 00:03:06.474
Before you write anything off.

00:03:06.474 --> 00:03:08.033
Before you say that that food

00:03:08.033 --> 00:03:09.099
is not going to be good for you,

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:10.373
or that activity is not
going to be good for you,

00:03:10.373 --> 00:03:12.561
at least try it, give it a shot

00:03:12.561 --> 00:03:15.004
and see if it feels right, and
see if you want to continue

00:03:15.004 --> 00:03:16.937
to push forward and learn more on it.

00:03:16.937 --> 00:03:18.553
But the most important thing, I think,

00:03:18.553 --> 00:03:22.116
is a self awareness to
figure out who you are,

00:03:22.116 --> 00:03:24.193
where you really want to
focus on, what you have

00:03:24.193 --> 00:03:26.919
Michael Jordan level talent at,

00:03:26.919 --> 00:03:29.931
and the ability to be
among the best in the world

00:03:29.931 --> 00:03:32.306
where you're going to apply
yourself, dedicate yourself,

00:03:32.306 --> 00:03:34.191
practice hard every single day.

00:03:34.191 --> 00:03:36.796
Figure out what it is that you can hop at

00:03:36.796 --> 00:03:40.222
and be that bunny for, and
go all in on that skill.

00:03:40.222 --> 00:03:42.081
And so the question of the day today is,

00:03:42.081 --> 00:03:44.339
I'm curious what are your
thoughts on public speaking?

00:03:44.339 --> 00:03:46.575
How good are you at
speaking, is it something

00:03:46.575 --> 00:03:49.090
that you want to get better
at, or are you totally

00:03:49.090 --> 00:03:50.957
going to disrespect it and
go focus on something else.

00:03:50.957 --> 00:03:52.414
I'd love to hear your thoughts.

00:03:52.414 --> 00:03:54.618
Please share down in the comments below.

00:03:54.618 --> 00:03:56.187
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Robb Barco.

