00:04:26.753 --> 00:04:30.557
- This is going to blow away
people, especially your fan base.

00:04:30.557 --> 00:04:31.390
Listening.

00:04:32.681 --> 00:04:35.034
You know, I speak a lot,
and I talk over people

00:04:35.034 --> 00:04:38.867
and I'm loud and intense
but all of my success

00:04:39.980 --> 00:04:42.462
has been predicated on
listening, whether I'm doing it

00:04:42.462 --> 00:04:44.336
with my ears, or with my eyes.

00:04:44.336 --> 00:04:47.849
- The skill I use is
probably communication.

00:04:47.849 --> 00:04:49.850
Which I think is building
on what Gary said.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:52.192
I think communication is a two way street,

00:04:52.192 --> 00:04:55.603
but being able to
articulate and communicate

00:04:55.603 --> 00:04:57.210
what it is that I'm trying to communicate,

00:04:57.210 --> 00:05:01.633
is something that I find
I focus on all day long,

00:05:01.633 --> 00:05:02.843
every time I speak.

00:05:02.843 --> 00:05:05.584
- How do you communicate authentically?

00:05:05.584 --> 00:05:08.394
How do you figure out what
to say and what not to say

00:05:08.394 --> 00:05:09.864
in a way that's authentic.

00:05:09.864 --> 00:05:12.329
And what Fred says, and I
really believe this is true,

00:05:12.329 --> 00:05:15.220
is it starts from the
fundamental understanding

00:05:15.220 --> 00:05:17.345
that there is no truth.

00:05:17.345 --> 00:05:18.694
There's my truth, there's your truth,

00:05:18.694 --> 00:05:20.303
that everything is subjective.

00:05:20.303 --> 00:05:22.499
And so if you always
start from the position of

00:05:22.499 --> 00:05:25.646
this is what I believe, I
don't expect you to believe it,

00:05:25.646 --> 00:05:27.013
I don't think you have to believe it,

00:05:27.013 --> 00:05:29.223
I'm not saying it's true,
you can actually always

00:05:29.223 --> 00:05:31.192
communicate authentically.

00:05:31.192 --> 00:05:33.162
Because if you walk in the
room, and this gets worse

00:05:33.162 --> 00:05:35.311
as you get more senior, here's the answer,

00:05:35.311 --> 00:05:38.272
you're not giving anyone else
any room to say anything.

00:05:38.272 --> 00:05:40.086
And if you walk into the room and say,

00:05:40.086 --> 00:05:44.708
I believe this for this
reason, what do you believe?

00:05:44.708 --> 00:05:48.174
If you share your truth in that language,

00:05:48.174 --> 00:05:50.847
you give people room to authenticate,

00:05:50.847 --> 00:05:52.334
to communicate authentically.

00:05:52.334 --> 00:05:55.242
And that is hugely important
to these relationships

00:05:55.242 --> 00:05:57.058
at any stage.

00:05:57.058 --> 00:06:01.225
- Connecting increases your
influence in every situation.

00:06:03.429 --> 00:06:05.281
For the foundation of the teaching today,

00:06:05.281 --> 00:06:07.419
I want to make sure that
we really have a grasp

00:06:07.419 --> 00:06:10.351
of why connecting with people is so vital.

00:06:10.351 --> 00:06:12.529
So if you go to the very
first sentence in your notes,

00:06:12.529 --> 00:06:14.999
the number one criteria for
advancement and promotion

00:06:14.999 --> 00:06:19.806
for professionals is an ability
to communicate effectively.

00:06:19.806 --> 00:06:21.701
That I do believe.

00:06:21.701 --> 00:06:24.433
I think the ability to
connect and communicate

00:06:24.433 --> 00:06:26.911
is the number one criteria
for success with your family,

00:06:26.911 --> 00:06:29.926
with your marriage, with your
children, with your friends,

00:06:29.926 --> 00:06:33.315
in the workplace, the
marketplace, in the community.

00:06:33.315 --> 00:06:36.379
If you have the ability
to connect with people,

00:06:36.379 --> 00:06:40.504
if can communicate and
connect, not just communicate,

00:06:40.504 --> 00:06:44.357
it takes you and literally
gives you a decided edge

00:06:44.357 --> 00:06:46.350
over others in the advancement

00:06:46.350 --> 00:06:48.106
in what we're trying to accomplish.

00:06:48.106 --> 00:06:51.684
For example, in your notes
Presidential historian

00:06:51.684 --> 00:06:55.810
Robert Alex says that the
successful President's

00:06:55.810 --> 00:06:59.093
exhibit five skills and
qualities that enable them

00:06:59.093 --> 00:07:02.291
to achieve things that others don't.

00:07:02.291 --> 00:07:04.516
So he's talking about
leaders and presidents

00:07:04.516 --> 00:07:07.097
and people, what makes some
achieve better than others.

00:07:07.097 --> 00:07:08.395
Here's the five things they do well.

00:07:08.395 --> 00:07:12.062
Number one is vision,
number two pragmatism,

00:07:14.271 --> 00:07:18.438
number three consensus
building; the ability to put

00:07:19.494 --> 00:07:22.239
together a team, get consensus.

00:07:22.239 --> 00:07:26.406
Number four, charisma, and
number five trustworthiness.

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.039
Being a trustworthy kind of a person.

00:07:33.039 --> 00:07:36.539
Now, what is interesting about these five,

00:07:37.472 --> 00:07:40.217
these five things that
set the better President's

00:07:40.217 --> 00:07:41.763
apart from maybe the average ones,

00:07:41.763 --> 00:07:44.930
four of the five deal with connecting.

00:07:46.105 --> 00:07:49.597
Vision is a definite connecting skill,

00:07:49.597 --> 00:07:51.722
the ability to cast a future vision.

00:07:51.722 --> 00:07:53.777
Consensus building, getting
people to work together,

00:07:53.777 --> 00:07:55.658
you have to be able to connect to do that.

00:07:55.658 --> 00:07:57.829
Charisma, of course, that's
why people follow the

00:07:57.829 --> 00:07:59.875
quote, the Pied Piper, and trustworthy.

00:07:59.875 --> 00:08:03.755
Four of the five of the
skills needed to be successful

00:08:03.755 --> 00:08:07.893
as a leader had a lot
to do with connecting.

00:08:07.893 --> 00:08:09.973
So let me define connecting,
because that's what this

00:08:09.973 --> 00:08:11.568
book is all about.

00:08:11.568 --> 00:08:15.796
Connecting is the ability
to identify with people

00:08:15.796 --> 00:08:20.152
and relate to them in such
a way that it increases

00:08:20.152 --> 00:08:22.152
our influence with them.

00:08:23.230 --> 00:08:25.624
In other words, we can identify
with them until they say,

00:08:25.624 --> 00:08:28.611
he or she understands exactly what I know

00:08:28.611 --> 00:08:30.769
and what I'm going
through, and we can relate

00:08:30.769 --> 00:08:33.433
with them until we,
because of that ability,

00:08:33.433 --> 00:08:35.974
we begin to increase
our influence with them

00:08:35.974 --> 00:08:38.240
and of course what do I teach
about leadership, very simple,

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:40.240
leadership is influence.

